---
/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * Written because the site collects email addresses through the contact and
 * sponsor forms and had no policy covering it, which is a problem today and a
 * blocker for AdSense tomorrow.
 *
 * IT DESCRIBES WHAT THE SITE ACTUALLY DOES, not what a template assumes. Right
 * now there is no analytics, no advertising and no third party script on any
 * page, and saying so plainly is worth more than boilerplate claiming
 * otherwise. The advertising section is written conditionally so it stays true
 * before AdSense is added and becomes true the day it is.
 *
 * When anything here changes, change this page in the same commit.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const updated = '13 September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy - Code with Sam"
  description="What Code with Sam collects, what it does not, and who else is involved when you use this site."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    This page describes what this site actually does with your data, rather than
    what a template assumes. Last updated {updated}.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This site does not run analytics, does not track you across the web, and
    sets no advertising or tracking cookies of its own. Nothing is requested
    from YouTube until you choose to play a video. The only personal data
    collected is an email address, and only when you choose to send one.
  </p>

  <h2>What is collected</h2>
  <h3>Messages you send</h3>
  <p>
    The contact and sponsor forms collect the email address and message you
    type. They are delivered through Web3Forms, which processes the submission
    and forwards it. The address is used to reply to you and for nothing else.
    It is not sold, rented or added to a mailing list without your asking.
  </p>

  <h3>The newsletter</h3>
  <p>
    If you give the newsletter form your email address, it is sent to Kit,
    which stores it on its own systems under its own privacy policy and is the
    only place it lives. Nothing is loaded from Kit until you submit the form,
    so simply reading this site sends Kit nothing at all. The address is used to
    send new articles and videos and for nothing else. Every email carries an
    unsubscribe link, and leaving removes the address.
  </p>

  <h3>Server logs</h3>
  <p>
    This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub receives the ordinary request
    information any web server receives, including your IP address, and handles
    it under GitHub's privacy statement. This is not something the site controls
    or can switch off.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no cookies of its own. It runs no analytics: there is no
    Google Analytics, no Tag Manager and no third party measurement script on
    any page.
  </p>

  <h3>YouTube</h3>
  <p>
    Articles show a still image rather than an embedded player, and nothing is
    requested from YouTube until you click to play. If you do play a video,
    YouTube may set cookies and receive data about that view under Google's
    privacy policy. Not playing a video means no contact with YouTube at all.
  </p>

  <h3>Advertising</h3>
  <p>
    This site currently shows no advertising. If advertising is introduced, this
    page will say so before it appears, and this section will name the provider
    and what it sets. Third party vendors, including Google, use cookies to
    serve ads based on prior visits to this and other websites. Google's use of
    advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your
    visits to this site and other sites. You can opt out of personalised
    advertising through
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">Google's Ads Settings</a>,
    and out of third party vendors' use of cookies at
    <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else is involved</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong>, hosting and server logs</li>
    <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong>, delivering contact and sponsor messages</li>
    <li><strong>YouTube</strong>, only if you press play</li>
    <li><strong>Kit</strong>, only if you submit the newsletter form</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Each handles data under its own policy. This site does not share your data
    with anyone beyond what is needed to deliver the thing you asked for.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Do not submit a form and no personal data is collected.</li>
    <li>Do not play a video and YouTube is never contacted.</li>
    <li>Ask for a copy of anything held about you, or ask for it to be deleted,
      through the <a href={`${base}/contact`}>contact page</a>.</li>
    <li>Browser settings can block cookies, including any set by a video you
      choose to play.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is aimed at working software engineers and is not directed at
    children under 13. No data is knowingly collected from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    When what the site does changes, this page changes with it, and the date at
    the top moves. There is no version of this page that describes something the
    site does not do.
  </p>
</Base>
